  "shape": "Serialised form of SECTIONS / ORDER / LOCALE_TEXT in scripts/qa/mockup-parity/section-map.mjs. Section keys are the data-w units of the mockup; `mockup` selectors address them by that attribute. `expects` are shared by both sides (the mockup is self-tested with the same rules). Product selectors use the anchors the Gridline design is planned to stamp (see ~/.claude/plans/gridline-build-plan.md, slice S3 to S7) and `data-parity-key` once the stable matching contract (5c) lands; until then a section whose anchor does not exist yet reports BLOCKED, never PASS.",
  "state": "planned: the Gridline design does not exist yet, so every product selector is a contract for the build slices, not an observed anchor.",
